---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../site.config.js';
---
<BaseLayout title="Advertising disclosure" description="How The Stat Method makes money: no paid placements, no advertising inside results, and affiliate disclosure above the links rather than buried in a footer.">
  <main class="prose-page">
    <h1>Advertising disclosure</h1>

    <h2>How this site makes money</h2>
    <p>
      Some links to products are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we may
      receive a commission from the retailer at no additional cost to you. Where a
      block of links is affiliate-based, it says so directly above the links —
      not in a footnote, and not after you have already clicked.
    </p>

    <h2>Reader donations</h2>
  <p>
    There is a Support button in the header and footer. It goes to a payment page
    hosted by Stripe, our payment processor — the same way the equipment links go
    to a retailer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two things worth stating plainly. <strong>Donating buys nothing.</strong> There
    is no members' area, no early access, no removal of anything, and no tool or
    article behind it. Everything on this site is free to everyone whether or not
    anybody ever donates, and that is not a limited-time position.
  </p>
  <p>
    And <strong>we do not receive your payment details.</strong> Your name, email,
    card and any message stay with Stripe. Nothing about a donation reaches this
    site, which has no database and no account system. We cannot see who donated,
    and we could not tell you if you asked. That is a deliberate design choice, not
    an oversight — it is what lets the privacy policy say we hold no personal
    information and mean it literally.
  </p>
  <p>
    Donations never influence what we recommend. A tool's result depends on the
    numbers you enter and the equation behind it, and there is no mechanism by
    which a payment could change either.
  </p>

  <h2>Rules we hold ourselves to</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Recommendations are not for sale.</strong> No manufacturer has
        ever paid to be included here, and none can. A commission does not
        influence whether something is recommended or how it is described.</li>
      <li><strong>No advertising inside results.</strong> Advertising never
        appears within, above, or beside a calculator's results, and never
        displaces a safety warning. Health information comes first and
        advertising fits around it, not the other way around.</li>
      <li><strong>Nothing is required.</strong> Every calculator on this site is
        free and complete without buying anything. Nothing in a gear
        recommendation is needed to get a result.</li>
      <li><strong>No health claims attached to products.</strong> We will not
        suggest that a product treats, prevents, or cures anything.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What advertisers learn about you</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing you type into a calculator, because that information never leaves
      your browser. If you follow an affiliate link, the retailer knows you came
      from this site — the same as any ordinary link. See our
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>FTC disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      United States Federal Trade Commission guidance requires that material
      connections between a publisher and a seller be disclosed clearly and
      conspicuously, near the recommendation rather than buried. That is why the
      affiliate notice sits directly above the links it applies to, in the same
      type size as the surrounding text, rather than in a footer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions about any of this:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
